    "answer": {
      "short": "Construction with $DC=5\\text{ cm}$ and $AB=BC=CD=DA=5\\text{ cm}$. All four sides are equal, so $ABCD$ is a rhombus.",
      "worked": "Draw $DC=5\\text{ cm}$ and follow the four construction steps, choosing $B$ as the intersection other than $D$.\n\n$DA=DC$ because $A$ lies on the circle with centre $D$ and radius $DC$.\n\n$AB=DC$ and $CB=DC$ because $B$ lies on the circles with centres $A$ and $C$, both of radius $DC$.\n\nTherefore $AB=BC=CD=DA=5\\text{ cm}$. A quadrilateral with four equal sides is a rhombus, so $ABCD$ is a rhombus.",
